# Design screenshots dropped into public/ — ignore the images, NOT the folder.
# A bare `public` entry excludes the directory itself, and git cannot re-include
# a file whose parent directory is excluded. Anything added to public/ later
# (robots.txt, a real favicon, _headers) would be missing from the deploy with
# no error anywhere: CI clones the repo, so what is not tracked is not built.
public/*.png
public/*.jpg
public/*.jpeg

# Local session/credential artifacts
login.json
*.cookies

# `> nul` is the cmd.exe null device, but the Bash tool runs Git Bash — there it
# is an ordinary relative path, so the redirect creates a junk file at the repo
# root instead of discarding the output. Anchored to `/` so it only covers that
# one spot (`nul` is a reserved name on Windows; nothing legitimate can be there).
/nul
